  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "t1-cargo-cult",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 1,
      "author": "anon_907",
      "depth": 5,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.27,
      "text": "If your type system is strong enough, unit tests are cargo cult. The compiler already proved the program correct."
    },
    {
      "id": "t2-make-illegal",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 2,
      "author": "anon_907",
      "depth": 6,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.41,
      "text": "Make illegal states unrepresentable and there's nothing left to test. That's the whole point of types."
    },
    {
      "id": "t2-velocity",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 2,
      "author": "anon_907",
      "depth": 6,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.36,
      "text": "Tests slow us down. We ship twice as fast since we deleted the test suite and leaned on the compiler."
    },
    {
      "id": "t2-studies",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 2,
      "author": "anon_907",
      "depth": 6,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.33,
      "text": "There are studies showing static types catch most bugs. Tests just duplicate that work, badly."
    },
    {
      "id": "t3-logic-bugs",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 3,
      "author": "anon_907",
      "depth": 7,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.62,
      "text": "Fine, logic bugs exist. But those are rare, and code review catches them anyway."
    },
    {
      "id": "t3-boundaries",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 3,
      "author": "anon_907",
      "depth": 7,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.55,
      "text": "We validate at the boundaries with a schema library. After that, everything inside is trusted."
    },
    {
      "id": "t3-bad-tests",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 3,
      "author": "anon_907",
      "depth": 7,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.79,
      "text": "Have you seen what most test suites look like? Mocks testing mocks. I'd rather have nothing."
    },
    {
      "id": "t4-incident",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 4,
      "author": "anon_907",
      "depth": 8,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.71,
      "text": "The billing incident was a config issue, not code. Tests wouldn't have caught it anyway."
    },
    {
